    <statement><p>Use algebra to evaluate the following limit.</p>
<p><m>\lim\limits_{h \rightarrow 0} \frac{(3+h)^2- 9  }{h} =</m>
<fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\frac{(3+h)^2- 9}{h} =
     \frac{3^2+6 h + h^2- 9}{h} =
	\frac{6 h + h^2}{h}=6+h</m>




Thus, as <m>h\to 0</m> we have
<m>\frac{(3+h)^2- 9}{h} \to 6</m>.



</solution>
